  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "King",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ab86178527114df990a97e4bf003874663c9fa71072ee3b6e32bd195b993f76f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ab8617852711-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 8,
                "start": 8
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "King argues that the judgment bar does not apply to a dismissal of claims raised in the same lawsuit because common\u2011law claim preclusion is not appropriate within a single lawsuit."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "King",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ab86178527114df990a97e4bf003874663c9fa71072ee3b6e32bd195b993f76f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ab8617852711-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "King further contends that the FTCA judgment bar is triggered only by \u201cthe judgment in an action under section 1346(b),\u201d and therefore does not bar the Bivens claim."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "King's Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ab86178527114df990a97e4bf003874663c9fa71072ee3b6e32bd195b993f76f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ab8617852711-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 13,
                "start": 13
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that the judgment bar provides that any order resolving an FTCA claim automatically precludes separate claims brought in the same action arising from the same common nucleus of facts."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ab86178527114df990a97e4bf003874663c9fa71072ee3b6e32bd195b993f76f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ab8617852711-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 15
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners note that referring to the entire lawsuit as \u201can action under section 1346(b)\u201d after the FTCA claims are decided would be strange, suggesting the bar should apply to the whole case."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners (Michael R. Huston)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Michael R. Huston), according to Petitioners (Michael R. Huston), in oral argument Michael R. Huston asserted that the FTCA judgment bar \u201cunambiguously precludes\u201d the Bivens action because the district court entered judgment in an action under \u00a71346(b)."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Huston",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            },
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Huston, the purpose of the judgment bar is repose; Congress intended the judgment in the FTCA action to bring finality to the entire controversy."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners' Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 64,
                "start": 64
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the Government characterizes the FTCA judgment bar as a simple common\u2011law doctrine of res judicata."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 65,
                "start": 65
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The Government argues that jurisdictional issues control, not merits, and that the judgment bar should apply regardless of the basis for the district court\u2019s dismissal."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Government's Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Jaicomo",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 35,
                "start": 35
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mr. Jaicomo argues that the judgment bar does not apply to claims brought together in a single action."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Mr. Jaicomo's Position",
